{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-52:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-52:a2fd19554327882df326b4fa477ef23faf61cb13cde7c6389708cd72aad70ade","timestamp":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.research.3w.linker.w1","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-52","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-52","title":"Links go to the reading queue: URL routing for bob capture, Bob Mac Capture, and bob gkeep pull","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.research.3w.linker.w1","updated_at":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"A bare public link lands in Bob's reading queue instead of becoming an inbox task. This covers a link captured with `bob capture` or Bob Mac Capture, whether alone, in a pasted list, or mixed with ordinary tasks, and a link shared to Google Keep and pulled with `bob gkeep pull`. Every path uses the same ingest engine as `bob ref create`. Capture stays instant, works offline, and never loses a link. The preview says honestly, without touching the network, whether the link is new or already in the library. Submit queues a durable ref job, and a detached background worker clips it. If a clip fails, the link falls back to exactly today's inbox task, plus a ⚠️ reason and a retry command. Keep pull clips inline and archives a note only after a terminal outcome. Bob Mac Capture presents the new reference item beautifully and parses nothing itself. Every path has an opt-out.","design":"plan:202610/url_capture_ref_routing.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202610/url_capture_ref_routing.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-52:000002:issue_created:bob-cli-52.1:4415348d0b9b1371705e4dd28b542865343376ca6f16782dcee506866a4f4f6a","timestamp":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.research.3w.linker.w1","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-52.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-52.1","title":"Typed, non-printing URL ingest extracted from bob ref create","status":"open","issue_type":"phase","parent_id":"bob-cli-52","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.research.3w.linker.w1","updated_at":"2026-10-07T12:11:16Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"ingest: extract a typed URL ingest API from `ref create`. It returns created, already-in-library, and already-queued outcomes, or a typed error kind with a retryable flag. It uses fixed reading-queue defaults, a machine-wide ingest lock, and fsync on install. `ref create` output and exit codes stay byte-identical. Also add the shared ⚠️ fallback-note helper.","design":"","model":"","size":"medium","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Epic plan plan:202610/url_capture_ref_routing.md defines phase ingest as one work unit","dependencies":[]}}}
